From 6e1a95a0d63fc82eb90c34abc463e0e7768ecc33 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Matheus Sampaio Queiroga <srherobrine20@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 18 Jul 2026 10:29:34 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] net: omci: add complete ITU managed entity name catalog

The agent currently assigns names only to the small subset of managed
entities that has dedicated local handling. All other standard classes are
exposed to userspace as a generic dynamic managed entity, even when their
class IDs are defined by OMCI.

Expand the existing lookup table with the managed entity names listed by
the Hack GPON MIB catalog, which consolidates the ITU-T G.984.4 and G.988
tables. Keep explicit fallbacks for future-standardization and
vendor-specific ranges.

This changes only metadata exported with MIB objects. It does not claim
protocol or datapath support for the newly named classes.

Signed-off-by: Matheus Sampaio Queiroga <srherobrine20@gmail.com>
---
